"""Layer-0 MLP unit 459 as an "already / has-been" detector.

The unit goes strongly negative on words that say something has happened
before the present moment: English "already" and "been"; "already" in other
languages (уже, đã, telah, déjà, bereits, już, già, すでに); the Chinese
perfect markers 已 / 已经 (already, has); and, more weakly, "previously",
"recently", "being", "'ve", 曾, 先, 又, 被 and similar. "been" is strongest
after "has" (or "'s"), weaker after "have", weakest after "had". Everywhere
else it is close to zero.

Predicted values are roughly the typical activation: -3.6 for "already"-type
words, -8 for 已/已经, -3.4 / -2.4 / -1.9 for "been" after has / have / had,
-1 for the weaker markers.
