"""Negative response to unmerged horizontal gaps and bare backslashes.

A one-space gap is strongest after another gap or a line break, moderate
following punctuation/operators, and nearly absent after words or numbers.
Tabs, nonbreaking spaces, and escape introducers follow the same distinction
at different strengths. Longer indentation runs have a smaller response.
The preceding gap length and escaped newlines refine the single-space case.
Only two preceding tokens are remembered; document boundaries reset memory.
This captures the large gap responses, leaving ordinary-text variation at zero.
"""

