demonstratives, and several other languages' third-person forms. Word spacing,
capitalization, and document starts affect the strength. 'Each other' is a
weak reciprocal, unlike 'other' used to introduce alternatives. The forms
his/her/its have a small negative response. Unlisted tokens return zero; the
document-end marker has its own response. This is a word-class approximation,
not a resolver of what the pronouns refer to.
