"""Script-based guess at a diffuse component.

layers.0.mlp.down_proj:485 is nearly silent: most of its activation is small noise, and
the large values sit on rare tokens with no shared meaning. The one pattern that holds
across the sample is by script:

- tokens containing CJK characters, or undecodable UTF-8 fragments, run slightly negative;
- whitespace and pure-digit tokens sit at zero;
- other tokens sit slightly negative, around the component's mean.

The rule explains only about 0.1% of the variance on training rows. It is included to show
what a readable, concept-based guess gets, not as a good model of the component.
